# Build artifacts
.pio/
.pioenvs/
.piolibdeps/
build/

# IDE files
.vscode/.browse.c_cpp.db*
.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/ipch
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Compiled files
*.o
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.uf2
*.map

# Device backups — a .bkp is a full LittleFS dump and carries /config/system.bin
# (Wi-Fi/MQTT/API secrets + password hashes). Never commit one. See finding C-1:
# scratchpad/backup_pre_ota/device.bkp was committed and leaked; purge it from
# history with git filter-repo and rotate the exposed credentials.
*.bkp

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Generated assets
WebUI_GZ.h
src/WebUI_GZ.h

# Generated docs
docs/MANUAL.html
docs/MANUAL.pdf
docs/MANUAL_with_images.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Test server certs (self-signed)
tools/test-server/certs/

# Test reports and logs (generated at runtime)
docs/test_reports/

# Screenshots (generated)
docs/screenshots_v2/
docs/screenshots_v4/

# Device runtime data (generated on-device)
data/history/
data/config/
# data/web holds the output of a per-env page diet (custom_fs_pages, see
# tools/build_webui_gz.py). Nothing in it is tracked, and from 2026-08-17
# nothing in it ships: a shipping image carries every page in flash, so these
# are build artifacts of the instrumented env alone — written by the build that
# asks for them, uploaded to the bench unit by hand.
#
# They were tracked for one release, while the release image depended on them.
# That is also the release where no zip actually carried them and /license
# shipped broken, which is the argument for not letting a user's image depend
# on a file that has to be deployed separately.
data/web/
# Contents, not the directory — git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation inside one never matches.
data/themes/*
# ...except the curated collection itself, which is authored source (built by
# tools/gen_theme_collection.py, contrast-audited) and is what docs/MANUAL.md
# links to. Only themes the device writes at runtime stay out.
!data/themes/*.thm
data/calib.csv
data/system.blog
data/system.old.blog
data/*.blog

# Claude Code (project config, may contain local paths)
.claude/

# Changelogs (auto-generated or versioned)
CHANGELOG_*.md

# Promotion (local only, not for the repo)
docs/promotion/
scratchpad/soak_a6.log

# Release zips are assets, not history: they go on the GitHub release, and the
# `release: vX artifacts` commit versions only the release/simut_{tft,alpha,pio}
# trees. A stray `git add release/` swept 17 MB of them in once — hence the rule
# rather than the convention alone. (The v1.6.x pair predates this and stays.)
release/simut_tft_v*.zip
release/simut_alpha_v*.zip
release/simut_pio_v*.zip

# local bench scratch
scratchpad/
